{"name":"Vineyard Autumn","hex":"#ee4455","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"vineyard","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A grape plantation, especially one used in the production of wine."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/vineyard"},{"term":"autumn","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Traditionally the third of the four seasons, when deciduous trees lose their leaves, and temperatures and daylight hours decrease; typically regarded as spanning the months of September, October, and November in the Northern Hemisphere, and the months of March, April and May in the Southern Hemisphere.","The time period when someone or something is past its prime."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To spend the autumn (in a particular place).","To (cause to) undergo the changes associated with autumn, such as leaves changing color and falling from trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/autumn"}],"entries":[{"title":"Vineyard","blocks":[{"text":"A vineyard is a plantation of grape-bearing vines. Many vineyards exist for winemaking; others for the production of raisins, table grapes, and non-alcoholic grape juice. The science, practice and study of vineyard production is known as viticulture. Vineyards are often characterised by their terroir, a French term loosely translating as \"a sense of place\" that refers to the specific geographical and geological characteristics of grapevine plantations, which may be imparted to the wine itself."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e5/Vineyards_in_Burgundy_France.jpg/330px-Vineyards_in_Burgundy_France.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vineyard"},{"title":"Autumn","blocks":[{"text":"Autumn, also known as fall in North American English, is one of the four temperate seasons on Earth. Outside the tropics, autumn marks the transition from summer to winter, beginning in September or March. Autumn is the season when the duration of daytime becomes noticeably shorter and the temperature cools considerably. Day length decreases and night length increases as the season progresses until the winter solstice in December and June. One of its main features in temperate climates is the striking change in colour of the leaves of deciduous trees as they prepare to shed."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d0/D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg/330px-D%C3%BClmen%2C_Wildpark_--_2014_--_3808_color_balanced.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autumn"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Vinepyrennees2.jpg/500px-Vinepyrennees2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Vinepyrennees2.jpg/500px-Vinepyrennees2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The extensive vineyards of the Languedoc-Roussillon region, southern France","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AVinepyrennees2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Aerial_View_-_Landschaft_Markgr%C3%A4flerland1.jpg/500px-Aerial_View_-_Landschaft_Markgr%C3%A4flerland1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Aerial_View_-_Landschaft_Markgr%C3%A4flerland1.jpg/1280px-Aerial_View_-_Landschaft_Markgr%C3%A4flerland1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6b/Aerial_View_-_Landschaft_Markgr%C3%A4flerland1.jpg/500px-Aerial_View_-_Landschaft_Markgr%C3%A4flerland1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Aerial view of vineyards in Ma